# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Test / coverage output
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# Built example binaries. Each `examples/<name>/` subdirectory is its
# own Go module; `go build` from inside one produces a binary named
# after the module (e.g. examples/as-rs-demo/as-rs-demo). The example
# is run with `go run .`, never installed — the binary is build
# output, not a source artifact. Whitelist source files so a future
# example sub-tree doesn't accidentally hide its `.go` or `.md`.
/examples/*/*
!/examples/*/*.go
!/examples/*/*.md
!/examples/*/go.mod
!/examples/*/go.sum
!/examples/*/testdata/
